# Always Add Tests

Whenever you change code, add or update tests that cover the change.

- Treat a change as incomplete until tests exist for the new or altered behavior
- Prefer colocated or existing project test patterns over inventing a new layout
- Cover the changed path: bug fixes need a regression test; features need happy-path and important edge cases
- Do not skip tests for "small" or "obvious" changes unless the edit is purely non-behavioral (comments, formatting, docs-only)
- Run the relevant tests after writing them and fix failures before finishing
